From c2c6e6eddfbf49abad185c808d7d1324b941d964 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Ferralis <ferralis@generalflash.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:24:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: draft angles on side faces (family and suite "draft")

Cast and moulded parts taper their side faces so they leave the mould. An intent "draft" tapers
faces by "angle" (degrees, 0.5-20) about the XY plane (z = 0), pulled along +Z, so outer faces lean
inward going up: every side face by default (planar faces parallel to Z and cylinders about Z; the
model issues the new Select:Faces|Z), or the faces named by points ("pts", Select:Face@Point). The
model then issues PartDesign_Draft, an upstream command that was only a distractor with a fixed
3 degrees; the runtime sets the angle, the neutral plane and the pull direction. New goal kind
"draft" (appended), the angle in the goal encoding's axis / angle block (no new numbers), the
Draft feature's angle in the state. New family and suite "draft": a box, cylinder, hexagon or
outline base, optional bosses on top, the draft (all side faces, or one or two faces of a box by
points), optionally a bore after it; angles stay small enough that every boss keeps half its size.
Earlier suites keep their goals.
